  "mechanical_findings": [
    "Two ranges are contiguous: [0,327155712) and [327155712,652195421); both STORED payload bytes are compared to retained original bytes by prepare, with per-range SHA/CRC and full-carrier SHA.",
    "Complete original prefixes and suffixes retain all differing local ZIP metadata, descriptors and central directory bytes; no ZIP repacking or reserialization occurs.",
    "All 13 non-payload members per carrier remain as independent original files and were fully read by this peer; these 26 reads plus all four literal reads matched the recipe.",
    "Prepare has no unlink or product execution. It observes regular single-link held descriptors, before/after identity and whole-source digest, then fsync/readback of the literal files.",
    "Corrected restore keeps O_RDWR output descriptor, handles short writes, fsyncs written bytes, independently preads full output SHA/size and checks the same inode/path identity before fchmod/utime on that descriptor and final parent fsync.",
    "Historical inode and ctime are explicitly not claimed for any reconstructed copy; content bytes and recorded mode/mtime can be restored.",
    "Original script defect retained in the review history: the prior restore only hashed the bytes submitted to write and changed mode/time by path. That point is fixed in the exact 5498-byte source now reviewed."
  ],
